WEBVTT

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.490
Hey! This is His Grace,
the Duke of Buckingham's--

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.200
Oh, Y-Your Majesty.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.870
All chambers belong to the king.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:24.870
But, um, His Grace
is absent at the moment.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.000
I doubt he'll return before morning.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.880
Patrol outside for a while.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.130
At once!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.720
Not before morning?

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.100
What's strange about that?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.810
Of course he'd rather spend the night
in someone else's company.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.280
I thought I'd gained everything.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.690
So why?

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.700
Why does golden slumber elude me?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.450
I want heat. That scalding heat.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.040
Who are your hands embracing now?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.880
I have no one but you
to embrace this body.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.010
Buckingham.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.640
Richard, what brings you here?

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.770
I'll be going.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.150
Return to your chambers, quickly.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.530
I said I would.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.320
You are a king.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.870
Why?

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.920
Buckingham, why are you so damp?

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.710
This way! Hurry!

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.640
York of the white rose.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.270
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:14.690
These royal houses with roses
for their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:19.820
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.880
Who are they?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.420
The players from the banquet.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.590
They acted the play that mocked the king.
Is he making an example?

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.550
I saw His Majesty give his man
an order at the time.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.810
His enemies perish before you know it.
An old trick of demons.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.610
So, what will Your Royal Majesty do now?

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:24.570
You can create an Eden and play
the saint at your next banquet,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.740
but these poor martyrs' deaths
will overshadow all your efforts.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.040
I look forward to the play's next act.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.710
Why are they together?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.470
He was merely passing time with a friend.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.600
Pardon me.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:53.560
His Majesty bids me remain at your side,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.690
given last night's killings.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:02.190
So, Richard does think of me sometimes.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:07.490
His Majesty is always
concerned for his queen.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.330
Then why couldn't he do his duty at night?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:19.580
Edward and I did ours, even without love.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.170
It was for our futures.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.170
You know him better than anyone.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.010
If he's hiding something, tell me!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.310
Back then, Richard leapt back,
as if to hide his body.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:43.480
What did I tell you?
Richard will never love you.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.650
Because Richard

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.070
is a woman.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.950
Mother.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:53.410
Father told me to join you.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.000
Edward.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.750
Yes. I see.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.960
I needn't worry.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.210
That could never be true.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:09.010
Your Majesty, pay no heed
to the idle chatter of the mob.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.010
Most likely, those fellows
fell out over their reward.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:17.140
No one else has a motive
for their killing.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:21.020
That man wasn't among the corpses.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.480
Do I worry too much?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.990
If there was a motive,
it was precisely this situation.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:33.030
It was a perfect opportunity
to pin the blame on His Majesty.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:36.410
You haven't worn your spectacles
since last night.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.460
I was careless.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.750
I'll have a new pair made.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:46.920
No, my king, I would rather
not see clearly now.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.670
I suppose not.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:59.180
Listen. The banquet will proceed
according to schedule.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:04.020
But first, deliver one of these letters
to every guest at once.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.030
Make sure every denizen of
"Richard's paradise" receives one.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.110
Nobles and servants.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.700
Soldiers and clerics.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.160
And of course, that man as well.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.750
"My dear actor,

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.540
Tonight, come to my paradise
as other than yourself.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.550
After Lucifer's Fall comes Adam and Eve."

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.300
A staple of festival plays, then.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.680
Take care, Lord Richmond.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:40.390
The Earl of Richmond has been
a fugitive since the Lancastrian defeat.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.560
I am but a traveling performer!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:48.980
But my lord, only you can restore
the House of Lancaster now.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:53.490
Please refrain from, um, rash actions.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.030
If I die, that too shall be God's will!

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.330
How silly.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.870
Fate is already determined.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:06.420
The Lord will choose me in the end.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.420
Still, what a bore!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.840
Come as "other than myself"?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:18.470
Our king, the Creator, must find
a fiend like me inconvenient.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.560
And really, who can blame him?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.190
If the devil came to his banquet,

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:30.320
it would spell the end of
Adam and Eve's beautiful Eden!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.490
What?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.200
Welcome to the demons' paradise.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.450
Demons?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.580
"Come as other than yourself."
There are no rules.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.290
You can become anything you wish.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.420
This is your paradise.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:56.590
Now, dance. Dance however you please.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.600
I've never had such fun at a banquet!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.140
It's a childhood dream come true!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.600
A toast to our new king!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.190
To King Richard III!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:10.070
To our king!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.070
Richard! Richard III!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.860
I like it!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.870
To this marvelous paradise!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.500
It's lovely, Richard.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.410
It wouldn't be worth taking otherwise.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.420
Richard.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.000
Are we Adam and Eve?

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.800
What do you mean?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.420
I want to ask you something.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.430
What is it?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.890
Come.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:42.140
Have you been hiding anything from me?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:47.640
Tell me, Richard! Why are we
the only ones who are still ourselves?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.770
If you have other costumes
prepared, tell me.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:57.240
We can't just go as the king and queen.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.490
I'm sorry, but I have none.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.580
Then we're in luck.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.200
You see, I have some ready here.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.080
I got us disguises.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:11.380
Disguises? They look
like ordinary clothes to me.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.090
Not that one.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.050
You'll wear this.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.680
The king and queen trade places.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.760
Doesn't it suit the theme perfectly?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.220
Don't tell me she noticed something then.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:29.810
If Richard really were a woman,

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.820
he would never appear as one in public.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.070
If you don't want to, say so.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.110
Do you have a reason
to avoid women's clothing?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.330
Mother!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.950
Will Father go in costume, too?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.750
Yes! Your father will be the queen.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:55.500
Your Majesty, if you have
nothing else, take my mask.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.800
I'd love to see that!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:02.640
Anne wouldn't test me if she was certain.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:15.520
I have no choice. A firm refusal
would only deepen her suspicions.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.530
How odd. I don't feel repulsed
like I did back then.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:26.580
Is that because it's a costume?
Or because I've become a demon?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:32.620
I never thought you'd end up
helping me to dress as a woman.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:35.290
If I'd been raised as a woman,

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.670
would you have helped me
into a dress like this every day?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:45.800
No, I doubt that I would have been
stationed at your side in that case.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.060
Oh, I suppose not.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.390
Excuse me.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:55.060
If I were a woman, everything
would have been different.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:01.070
But my beloved father called me his son,

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.110
so that alone became my pride.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.540
Mother, you look so dashing!
It's wonderful!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:14.920
Richard looked as though he had
to be pressured into wearing it.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.880
Still, I'm sure I've been
worried for nothing.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.300
I mean, it simply couldn't be true.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:24.760
Anne.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.980
Will this do?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.490
I've never seen anyone
so beautiful before!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.660
Is it too obvious who I am?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.710
I should have worn a mask after all.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.040
No wonder Edward got confused.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.170
Even my body feels so hot
just being near her.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.550
What's gotten into me?

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.720
Why does she seem so beautiful?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.600
I beg your pardon, madam.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.940
Would you care to dance with us?

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.770
N-No, he--<i>she</i>--is with me.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:23.070
Why, sir! None of us
are ourselves tonight!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.150
His Majesty commands it.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.360
Let's dance.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.700
Let's all forget about birth and names!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.120
If...

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.580
If I weren't...

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.500
If I weren't Richard, then...

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.470
Stand aside, shepherd.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.680
Now, let's go.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.510
Where have I...?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.930
No, I wouldn't recognize him
even if we had met.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.890
That goes for everyone tonight.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.520
I'll dance with this beauty!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.940
No, I will!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.730
I've been waiting longer!

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.440
Back off! She'd never choose you!

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.110
Now, my lady!

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.320
Make your choice!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.910
Who? Who am I looking for?

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:17.660
Come on, Richard.
You've got to find them soon.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:21.790
You have everything now,
so what are you afraid of?

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.670
Who will you choose?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.590
--Who?
--Who?

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.630
Who?!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.840
Who will I...?

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.260
A demon!

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.930
It's a demon!

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.520
You remind me of someone I know.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.820
This voice.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.610
These hands.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.950
This warmth.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:54.160
Buckingham. I've been
looking for you all this time.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:03.080
It's simple. I don't put my soul
into words spoken for a woman.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:07.510
But I can never speak the truth.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:13.180
Even if I love so madly that my
soul's hellfire threatens to consume me.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.220
Thank goodness you aren't
who you remind me of.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.640
I would never want to let you go
again if you were.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.560
No. I refuse.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.980
I'll never let you release me again!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.650
Don't go!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.280
You can't be...

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.530
Richard!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:36.030
I'm not Richard,
and you aren't yourself either.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.490
Not tonight.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:40.960
The beauty left with the devil.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.830
If that was her costume,
what is she normally?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.590
Richard.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.130
Wait a moment.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.930
Where are we going?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:56.510
I don't care, as long as no one
recognizes us as a king and a duke.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.810
Just tonight.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.270
It's just for tonight.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.320
How far do you intend to ride?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.070
Further than this.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:19.950
To somewhere where we can escape
from this whole world.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:22.750
We'll be alone in these woods.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.460
Hey! Stop the horse! We'll crash!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.090
No subjects, nobles, or kings.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.250
Richard!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.010
Richard!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.680
Do you want to die?!

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:47.440
Is that how the king you made
makes you look?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.820
Does he fear losing everything he's built?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.120
Or does he...

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.490
Why did you make me realize?

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:04.210
I may deny it with my mind,
but I can never again claim...

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.710
...that I have never loved anyone.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.010
Look.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:18.340
We were in a field of roses
when we made our pact as well.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.270
I can never go back.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.770
Not now that I realize the truth.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:31.690
We're the same.
That's what you told me then.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.450
Yes, I did.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.160
We want the same thing.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.950
Say it. Tell me your desire.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.330
In truth, I've always...

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:51.130
...from the very beginning, I've...

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.130
Richard, I want you.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.760
You belong to me.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.830
We'll take ill if we
fall asleep like this.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.420
I wouldn't mind freezing to death
if you're with me.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.380
Return in my clothes.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:39.300
Don't be ridiculous.
My brother kept a house near here.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.970
Its caretaker should be absent tonight.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:46.060
By the way, why were
you dressed like this?

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.770
Anne and Edward begged me.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.390
Are you hurt?

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.440
I don't have my glasses.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.520
Here.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.610
Don't let go.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.070
Never let go of my hand.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:07.790
The night forest is always looking
for a chink in your warmth.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.750
I wonder where Father went.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.550
A boar?

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.430
Maybe I imagined it.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:30.770
I beg your pard--

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.480
Who is he?

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:39.030
Might you be King Richard's son?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.360
Y-Yes.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.610
You don't look like him.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:48.200
You're nothing alike, from the color
of your hair to the tips of your toes.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.160
It makes me wonder:

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.460
Are you really his son?

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:55.080
What?

00:19:55.080 --> 00:20:00.210
If your father was actually some man
from who knows where,

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:02.550
then that rumor might be true.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.970
F-Father?

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:09.560
Sorry, but I'm not your father.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.480
Elizabeth! What are you doing here?

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.480
I told you to call me Beth, remember?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.400
Elizabeth.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.070
The late king's daughter.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.460
I never thought I'd see this place again.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.500
You were my only salvation.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:42.010
This place where I spent
that time with him.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.970
Where are the clothes?

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:47.510
I'll fetch them while you warm yourself.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.140
You don't need much looking after.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.350
Who do you take me for?
I'm no longer a child.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.770
Who am I comparing him to?

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.480
It can't be.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.190
Is something wrong?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:03.740
You've been odd since
we came to this house.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.610
Are you well?

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:10.080
Nothing's wrong. I'm fine, Buckingham.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.700
Yes. He's different.

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.460
Richard,

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:20.800
won't you call me by
my real name now, not my title?

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.260
My name.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.300
Your name.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:29.470
Yes. Henry Stafford.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.850
Call me Henry.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.430
But it's just so...

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:43.730
Just so much like that day,
which will never come again.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:49.200
Are you here?
